    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "A proposed amendment of approved specs 029 and 041 (and of spec 006's command table through 029 3.13), for release 0.4.1. Today `rustev gate select` reads only repeat sets Rustev evaluated itself: every run is a spec 004 evaluation of a Rustev plan over a Rustev dataset manifest. A host whose baseline and candidate runs execute in its own runtime, and whose outputs are scored through `scoreViews` into `rustev.scores/1`, has no supported way in. This spec adds a host run record (`rustev.host-run/1`) carrying host dataset, flow, version and run identities with per-case outcomes, latency and cost; an import command, `rustev eval repeat import`, that verifies the host's views and scores and builds a host repeat set with spec 029's statistics; a host baseline; and selection over host sets. Host documents have their own schema names, so no existing document changes bytes or meaning and a host set can never be compared with a Rustev-evaluated one. Every figure is labeled host-asserted. Ratified (A-77) for release 0.4.1.\n",
    "title": "Host-scored repeat sets for the selection gate (amends 029 and 041)"
